Ultra WoW's opcodes for AzerothCore (0x521-0x556)

Ultra WoW (x64 and 32-bit) sends opcodes of its own once a player is in the world: spell charges,
retail item variants, radial pings, skyriding, Mythic+ (challenge modes), loot specialization,
toasts, quest helpers, weekly rewards, the wardrobe and transmog outfits, the appearance protocol,
area loot, garrison, Paragon, and 0x556 for loot beams. AzerothCore knows opcodes up to 0x520 and
closes the connection on any other. This patch names them in Opcodes.h, moves NUM_MSG_TYPES from
0x521 to 0x557 (every table and bound that uses it grows with it) and gives each a table entry in
Opcodes.cpp: the client opcodes STATUS_UNHANDLED (queued, then dropped with a debug log line - a
server module answers the ones it handles), the three appearance hello/prepare/query opcodes
STATUS_AUTHED with Handle_NULL, every server opcode STATUS_NEVER. Nothing else changes; clients
that never send them see no difference.

Apply in the AzerothCore source folder (the one with src\ and modules\), then build the worldserver:
    git apply --check ultra-wow-opcodes.patch      (prints nothing when it fits)
    git apply ultra-wow-opcodes.patch
Made 2026-10-29 against AzerothCore (the playerbots fork; the two files as AzerothCore had them
since 2026-07-27).

It changes AzerothCore's code, so it is under AzerothCore's licence: the GNU General Public License,
version 2.

